{
  "_comment": "Recommended baseline Claude Code permissions for macOS and Windows — a SAFE, conservative default. Copy the `permissions` object into your own ~/.claude/settings.json (global) or a project .claude/settings.json, MERGING with any permissions you already have. Precedence is deny > ask > allow, and anything not listed still prompts. Bash(...) rules cover the Bash tool (macOS, Linux, Git Bash); PowerShell(...) rules are their Windows twins. Bash/PowerShell ask and deny rules match the usual spelling of a command — they are tripwires, not a security boundary. This is a hand-copied template, not an auto-installed file, and it contains NO secrets or machine-specific paths. See README 'Recommended permissions' for what each group does and for optional add-on groups (build tools, language runtimes, file-mutation, etc.) you can opt into. Remove this _comment key before use (settings.json is strict JSON).",
